    "body": "The maintainer gave a reproduction in chat on 2026-11-17: a project of his own with one setup (WCS G54), a stock, a self-centering vise as a fixture, one model and two 2D Adaptive operations (source: stock, one closed chain of 94.2 mm), on build 0.23.0 `ea97d63b`. The project file stays private. The worker reads it locally and makes a fixture of its own for the tests.\n\nWhat his screenshot shows:\n- The viewport draws two axis triads. One has the label G54 and is at a corner above the part. The other has no label and is lower, near the part and the vise.\n- The toolpath is drawn in a hole at the top of the part. The ring of the selected chain is drawn lower and to the side of it. The toolpath and the picked geometry are not at the same place.\n- The operation status is OK with 2102 moves and names a position (-75.27, 76.27).\n\nTo find: which frame each of these uses (the chain display, the generation input, the toolpath display, the posted X Y Z), and if the seat of the stock on the vise or a model transform moved the part and the WCS or the toolpath did not follow.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
