    "updated_at": "2026-11-17T21:43:36Z",
    "body": "Reproduction (issue-worker-high, branch `issue/2382-wcs-origin`).\n\n**Readings from the reporter's project** (a local copy, read headlessly, not attached):\n- G54 is on a stock corner, far from the world origin. The setup alignment turns the part -90 degrees about Z.\n- The toolpaths are in the setup frame and stand on the aligned part. The holes and the cut areas are correct.\n- The first move of each operation is a rapid from X0 Y0 at the clearance height. That point is the world origin, not G54.\n- The project posts with a refusal that is not related to this issue: \"Home1: 2D Adaptive1 Copy already ends with Pause (M0)\". I did not change the project. The posted reading below comes from a minimal fixture.\n\n**Where the defect shows:**\n- Viewport: the opening rapid is drawn from the world origin.\n- Simulation: the link between operations starts at the first move's start, which is the world origin.\n- CL text: the `START` line is the world origin.\n- Post engine: `StartX/Y/Z` of the first move is the world origin.\n- Posted G-code blocks: correct. A post writes only the end of each move, and each end is measured from G54. The fixture test confirms that no block goes to the world origin.\n\n**Cause (found by reading):**\n- Most mill generators seed their path builder at `Point3::new(0.0, 0.0, clearance_z)`: the frame zero, which is the world origin.\n- Since 942a36d65 (#690 / #697, v0.17) the opening rapid starts from that seed.\n- This is not a 0.23 regression. It shows more now, because setups place the part far from the world origin (alignment, vise seating #2173).\n\n**Families that use the world origin seed:**\n- 2D: face, contour, contour chain, pocket, adaptive rest, bore, chamfer, circular, slots, thread ride, trochoidal slot, 2D rest.\n- 3D finishing: raster/parallel, flat, pencil, polar, rings, flow, morph, geodesic, shadow, deburr.\n- Multi-axis: 5-axis contour and parallel (they stamp a finishing path).\n\n**Families that do not use it:**\n- Hole: drilling seeds at the first hole.\n- 3D roughing: seeds at its first entry.\n- Adaptive trochoidal: seeds at its first entry.\n- Plasma: seeds at the pierce point.\n- Sinker EDM: seeds at its own X Y.\n- Turning: seeds at its own station.\n- Wire: starts at its own first point.\n- Multi-axis rotary and curve: seed at the first tool point.\n\n**Fix plan:** after generation, move the start of the opening rapid to the setup's WCS origin (from `wcs_context`, the same origin that the post subtracts). The end of that rapid does not change, so no posted block changes. A 3+2 path reads the origin in its local frame.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
